<title>NEW ZEALAND: Cultus 1st half net falls to A$3.43 mln.</title>
<headline>Cultus 1st half net falls to A$3.43 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to December 31.</p>
<p>			   (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    3.43 vs 4.91</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   2.01 vs 2.97</p>
<p>    Turnover			     37.62 vs 27.40</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			 8.58 vs 5.62</p>
<p>    Abnormals before tax	debit 4.18 vs 0.71 debit</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.98 vs nil</p>
<p>Note - Cultus Petroleum Ltd is an oil and gas producer. Its major shareholders are New Zealand bankers Michael Fay and David Richwhite, who own 30 perent of the issued capital.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
